---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: "Foundations"
summary: "The framework we use to evaluate institutions, plus a separate shelf of philosophy and political theory."
type: page
---
{% from "partials/card.njk" import card with context %}
<div class="wrap">
  <header class="page-header">
    <p class="eyebrow">Framework and philosophy</p>
    <h1>Foundations</h1>
    <p class="lede">{{ summary }} These pieces are kept apart from the practical policy work so each can be judged on its own terms.</p>
  </header>

  <section aria-labelledby="rubric-heading">
    <h2 id="rubric-heading">The evaluation rubric</h2>
    <p>Condensed from Articles 1–7 of <em>The Alignment Manifesto</em>. Used to score every bill, brief, and court practice on this site.</p>
    <ol class="rubric-list">
      {% for r in site.rubric %}<li><strong>Article {{ r.article }}.</strong> {{ r.question }}</li>{% endfor %}
    </ol>
    <p class="callout callout--note"><strong>Test question:</strong> {{ site.rubricTest }}</p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="shelf-heading">
    <h2 id="shelf-heading">The shelf</h2>
    <div class="card-list">
      {% for item in collections.foundations %}
        {{ card(item) }}
      {% else %}
        <p class="empty">Forthcoming.</p>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </section>
</div>